StoreStatuspageRequest.description:
Create a status page. Without `slug`, a unique slug is derived from the name. The page
starts with public access and is published right away when your plan has a free slot;
otherwise it is created unpublished. Publishing and unpublishing have their own endpoints.

get.description:
The live source for building a valid `settings.config` payload for
`POST /v1/services`. `data` is keyed by check-type slug, one entry per type you
can create: `http`, `tcp`, `dns`, `icmp`, `ssl`, `manual`. Per check type:

- `key`, `label`, `description` — identity.
- `target_required` — whether a `target` must be sent (passive types like
  `manual`/`heartbeat` are `false`).
- `fields` — the `settings.config` fields: `{ name, type, label, required,
  secret, options?, default?, help? }`. `secret: true` marks a field whose
  value is encrypted at rest and never returned: it reads back as
  `__LIVCK_KEEP_UNCHANGED__`, and sending that value in an update keeps it.
- `conditions` — the assertion catalog: `fields[]` (`{ field, label, type,
  operators[], unit? }`) lists the assertable fields and their operators,
  `defaults[]` the conditions applied when none are supplied, and
  `by_subtype` (when present) restricts which fields apply per subtype
  (e.g. DNS record type).
- `interval` — `{ default, min, max }` seconds, when the type bounds it.

Built from the same definitions the API validates against, so it is always current.

Example (truncated):

```json
{
  "data": {
    "http": {
      "key": "http",
      "label": "HTTP(S)",
      "target_required": true,
      "fields": [
        { "name": "method", "type": "select", "required": false, "options": ["GET", "POST"], "default": "GET" }
      ],
      "conditions": {
        "fields": [
          { "field": "status_code", "type": "integer", "operators": ["eq", "gte", "lte"] }
        ],
        "defaults": [
          { "field": "status_code", "operator": "gte", "value": 400, "status": "down" }
        ]
      },
      "interval": { "default": 60, "min": 30, "max": 3600 }
    }
  }
}
```

post.description:
Send the file as multipart form field `file`. `asset` is one of `logo`,
`logo-dark`, `favicon`. Logos accept jpg/jpeg/png/webp/svg (≤2 MB);
favicons accept ico/png/svg (≤1 MB).

put.description:
The document is written WHOLE — every key you omit is removed, including locales
inside a translatable block (`title`, `body_md`, `heading`, `label`, `text` accept
either a plain string or a `{locale: value}` object). Send the complete desired
state, which is what the layout editor in the web app does too.

`sections` is the render order. Core sections (`status_banner`, `maintenance`,
`component_tree`, `metrics`, `active_incidents`) render your real data and may
appear at most once; `status_banner` is mandatory. Custom sections (`intro`,
`link_group`, `announcement`, `rich_text`, `spacer`, `divider`) carry your own
structured content in `config` — validated per type, never raw HTML/CSS/JS.

Example (an "unofficial demo" banner above everything else):

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "demo-note",
      "type": "announcement",
      "config": {
        "tone": "warning",
        "body_md": { "de": "Unverbindliche Demo.", "en": "Non-binding demo." }
      }
    },
    { "id": "status_banner", "type": "status_banner" },
    { "id": "component_tree", "type": "component_tree" }
  ]
}
```

Requires the `custom_branding` plan feature (403 otherwise).
